<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> This SCP is an anomalous event in a gas station, where if an individual looks at the bathroom's mirror for enough time they will be controlled and later killed by their reflection.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> An SCP Foundation Researcher is driving in his car to his house, he suddenly sees a gas station and stops there to wash his face. He enters the bathroom and begins realizing this gas station was never here before, hence why he didn't recognize it. As he was washing his face, the Researcher began looking intently at the mirror and started scratching his arm uncontrollably, grabbed his hair and breathed heavily, showing signs of paranoia, then suddenly began acting against his own will and followed his reflection's movement. After a bit, the reflection smiled and grabbed a hammer, so did the Researcher, they both swung the hammer towards the mirror, shattering it, and the Staff member dropped dead in the bathroom with multiple cuts around his body. The Foundation later found the body and started studying the SCP, theorizing it's origin and it's containment.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The gas station is often moved between places and awaits for it's next victim, and what's interesting to note is that the individual starts becoming their own reflection and begins following it's movement. It swaps the real person with the reflection, which can't escape the mirror and can only kill others.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> The SCP manipulates and kills people in the same way every time, however the anomaly doesn't work if multiple people are witnessing, which is why it mostly targets one or two people. After the mirror is shattered and the individual is dead, the gas station will move locations which leaves the body on the ground in the location of the murder and rebuilds the mirror instantly.</p>

