			<div class="content" id="post-content-4824971">
									

<p><strong>DISCLAIMER: I am a newbie and I can't give green-lights.</strong><br />
<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Take my advice with a large grain of salt</span>.</strong></p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">I'm leaving this here temporarily, I shall add critique below this as soon as I am able to.</span></p>
<p>Ello there! So there's quite a bit I really enjoy about this, and then there is some stuff I'd like to give advice on.</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">I'll start off with what I thought was really good about this concept.</span></p>
<p>1. I really love how your SCP is setup, it's simple and to the point. It makes it really easy to come across and understand.</p>
<p>2. I also really like the concept, it's one that can lead to a lot when it comes to storytelling of the Foundation staff or people around the SCP. The fact that the SCP moves between different places with not many restrictions means that your story is not constrained from one part physical world. This means you can add lore and interviews revolving around the SCP from multiple different places. Heck, I'd say go one step further and add some wackiness in there. If the SCP isn't restricted to being in a place like a city, have one of the reported locations that it was found in be something crazy like in the middle of a uninhabited desert.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Now I do have some things I'd like to address that I'm quite confused on.</span></p>
<p>1. Try being more specific about how the SCP operates. I especially think you need to give some more detail into the &quot;gas station&quot; part of the SCP itself.</p>
<ul>
<li>What kind of gas station is it? Is it of a specific custom brand or does it change randomly between other gas station brands to help its manipulation?</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>Does the gas station change its products, shape, and pricing based on where it's located or is it the same no matter where it is?</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>Does the SCP have any restrictions to where it changes its location? Can it appear in any part of the world or does it only spawn in areas like cities and common gas-station locations? I get that you described in the findings that the SCP was &quot;never there before&quot; according to the staff researcher, but you got to give more detail into where it &quot;moves between places&quot;.</li>
</ul>
<p>2. How does the Foundation know about these findings? According to your story, the body of the staff member was found, but that doesn't describe to the Foundation what exactly happened.</p>
<ul>
<li>If the Foundation can't find the gas station (since it moves after the mirror is shattered) how does the Foundation know that the staff member was even killed by an anomalous entity?</li>
</ul>
<p>I recommend giving more explanation into this. Here's some ideas I can give:</p>
<ul>
<li>Have the Foundation ask other staff in the local area of any sudden changes.</li>
<li>Have the Foundation spot a correlation between multiple discoveries of the same kind of events.</li>
</ul>
<p>EDIT: Sorry for typos and bad syntax, I was using a phone earlier when reviewing this.</p>
