			<div class="content" id="post-content-4825006">
									

<p>Hey, thank you for the feedback, I'll be sure to answer your questions! Ok, the gas station doesn't have any custom unique features to it, it's a normal gas station that you would find on the road, sometimes it can adapt to it's area to make it more natural but it's pretty much just an ordinary gas station.</p>
<p>It's mostly the same usually, the products are only changed if they don't exist or aren't really common in the area and the prices are the normal price the product would have. The gas station's shape will always stay the same.</p>
<p>The area doesn't really matter much, the SCP only moves itself to places where it's target will go by and stop to take a quick break, but it's obvious it can only appear somewhere where it fits, it can't just appear randomly inside of a building.</p>
<p>The Foundation didn't of course know at first this was a gas station SCP that murdered the Staff member, but they were aware of the possibility of an SCP, so after that the Foundation started sending Field Agents to investigate on anomalies that could be happening. After gathering more info, Staff members started theorizing on it's containment and later would successfully contain it by having 4 or 5 guards take shifts to stay and secure the area so no anomaly occurs and the gas station moves somewhere or the mirror affects anyone.</p>
<p>I will take those into account, I really do appreciate your thoughts and if any more questions or ideas come up tell me, thank you.</p>

